

1. Introductory Clause

SOLUTION:

Thinkplus Investments Limited (the Lender) and GreenTech Innovations Limited (the Borrower), hereinafter jointly referred to as the "Parties," have agreed to enter into this Loan Agreement for the purpose of the Lender lending the sum of £5,000,000 (the "Principal Amount") to the Borrower, for the purpose of expanding their renewable energy projects in London, United Kingdom. This Loan Agreement is made on the date of execution hereof (the "Effective Date").

2. Loan Terms

2. Loan Terms

The Parties agree that the following terms shall apply to the Loan:

(a) Loan Amount: The Lender shall lend to the Borrower the Principal Amount of £5,000,000 in the currency of British Pounds Sterling.

(b) Maturity: The term of the Loan shall be ten (10) years, commencing on the Effective Date.

(c) Repayment: The Borrower shall repay the Principal Amount, together with any accrued interest, on the maturity date of the Loan.

(d) Interest: The Borrower shall pay interest on the Principal Amount at a rate of 5% per annum, calculated on a simple interest basis.

(e) Security: The Borrower shall grant the Lender a first charge over all its assets as security for the Loan.

(f) Drawdown: The Borrower may request a drawdown of the Principal Amount from the Lender in tranches, subject to the Lender's approval.

(g) Use of Proceeds: The Borrower shall use the proceeds of the Loan solely for the purpose of expanding their renewable energy projects in London, United Kingdom.

(h) Currency: All payments under this Loan Agreement shall be made in British Pounds Sterling.

(i) Governing Law: This Loan Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of England and Wales.

(j) Jurisdiction: The courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any disputes arising out of or in connection with this Loan Agreement.

3. Interest and Fees

3. Interest and Fees

(a) Interest:

The Borrower shall pay interest on the Principal Amount at a rate of 5% per annum, calculated on a simple interest basis. Interest shall accrue from the Effective Date and shall be payable in equal monthly installments on the first day of each calendar month.

(b) Fees:

The Borrower shall pay the Lender the following fees:

(i) Commitment Fee: The Borrower shall pay the Lender a commitment fee equal to 0.25% of the Principal Amount for each month that the Loan is outstanding, payable quarterly in arrears.

(ii) Arrangement Fee: The Borrower shall pay the Lender an arrangement fee equal to 1% of the Principal Amount, payable on the Effective Date.

(iii) Legal Fee: The Borrower shall pay the Lender's reasonable legal fees and expenses incurred in connection with this Loan Agreement, payable on demand.

4. Default and Remedies

4. Default and Remedies

(a) Default:

If the Borrower fails to make any payment when due, or breaches any other term or condition of this Loan Agreement, such failure or breach shall constitute an event of default.

(b) Remedies:

Upon the occurrence of an event of default, the Lender shall have the following remedies:

(i) Acceleration: The Lender may demand immediate payment in full of the Principal Amount, accrued interest, and all other amounts owing under this Loan Agreement.

(ii) Security: The Lender may exercise any rights and remedies available to it under the Security Agreement, if any.

(iii) Legal Action: The Lender may institute legal proceedings against the Borrower to recover any amounts owing.

(c) Additional Remedies:

The remedies listed above are cumulative and not exclusive. The Lender shall have the right to pursue any other remedies available to it under applicable law.

(d) Notice:

The Lender may give notice to the Borrower of any default, and such notice shall not affect the Lender's right to exercise any remedies available to it.

(e) Waiver:

The failure of the Lender to exercise any right or remedy under this Loan Agreement shall not constitute a waiver of such right or remedy. Any waiver by the Lender of a default or breach of this Loan Agreement shall not operate as a waiver of any subsequent default or breach.

(f) Time of Essence:

Time shall be of the essence in the performance of all obligations under this Loan Agreement.

(g) Governing Law:

This section shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of England and Wales.

(h) Jurisdiction:

The courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any disputes arising out of or in connection with this Loan Agreement.

5. Representations and Warranties

5. Representations and Warranties

