The Borrower represents and warrants to the Lender as follows:

(i) Existence and Authority: The Borrower is a duly incorporated and validly existing limited company under the laws of England and Wales, and has the power and authority to enter into and perform its obligations under this Loan Agreement.

(ii) Authorization: This Loan Agreement has been duly executed and delivered by the Borrower, and constitutes the legal, valid, and binding obligation of the Borrower, enforceable against the Borrower in accordance with its terms, except as may be limited by bankruptcy, insolvency, or other laws of general applicability.

(iii) No Conflicts: The execution, delivery, and performance of this Loan Agreement do not conflict with any other agreement to which the Borrower is a party or by which it is bound.

(iv) Borrowing Authority: The Borrower has full power and authority to pledge and hypothecate the Loan Proceeds and the security therefor as provided in this Loan Agreement.

(v) No Default: As of the date of this Loan Agreement, there is no default or event of default under any agreement to which the Borrower is a party or by which it is bound.

(vi) No Litigation: As of the date of this Loan Agreement, there is no pending or threatened litigation or governmental action that could materially and adversely affect the Borrower's ability to perform its obligations under this Loan Agreement.

(vii) Financial Statements: The financial statements of the Borrower submitted to the Lender are true and complete in all material respects.

(b) Lender's Representations and Warranties:

The Lender represents and warrants to the Borrower as follows:

(i) Existence and Authority: Thinkplus Investments Limited is a duly incorporated and validly existing limited company under the laws of England and Wales, and has the power and authority to enter into and perform its obligations under this Loan Agreement.

(ii) Authorization: This Loan Agreement has been duly executed and delivered by the Lender, and constitutes the legal, valid, and binding obligation of the Lender, enforceable against the Lender in accordance with its terms, except as may be limited by bankruptcy, insolvency, or other laws of general applicability.

(iii) No Conflicts: The execution, delivery, and performance of this Loan Agreement do not conflict with any other agreement to which the Lender is a party or by which it is bound.

(iv) No Default: As of the date of this Loan Agreement, there is no default or event of default under any agreement to which the Lender is a party or by which it is bound.

(v) No Litigation: As of the date of this Loan Agreement, there is no pending or threatened litigation or governmental action that could materially and adversely affect the Lender's ability to perform its obligations under this Loan Agreement.

(vi) Authority to Grant Loan: The Lender has all necessary power and authority to make the Loan and grant the security therefor.

6. Covenants

SECTION:

6. Covenants

(a) Borrower's Covenants:

The Borrower covenants and agrees as follows:

(i) Use of Proceeds: The Borrower shall use the Loan solely for the purposes of expanding their renewable energy projects in London, United Kingdom.

(ii) Payment of Interest: The Borrower shall pay the interest on the Loan on the due dates as set forth in Section 3.

(iii) Payment of Principal: The Borrower shall repay the principal amount of the Loan, together with any accrued and unpaid interest, on the maturity date.

(iv) Maintenance of Financial Condition: The Borrower shall maintain a satisfactory financial condition and shall provide the Lender with such financial statements and information as the Lender may reasonably request.

(v) Notice of Events: The Borrower shall promptly notify the Lender of any material adverse change in its financial condition, business, or operations.

(vi) Compliance with Laws: The Borrower shall comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and governmental orders, and shall obtain all necessary permits, licenses, and approvals.

(vii) No Encumbrances: The Borrower shall not create any liens, encumbrances, or security interests on the Collateral without the prior written consent of the Lender.

(b) Lender's Covenants:

The Lender covenants and agrees as follows:

(i) No Offset: The Lender shall not set off any amounts owed to the Borrower against the Loan or any interest thereon.

(ii) No Waiver: The Lender's failure to exercise any right or remedy under this Loan Agreement shall not constitute a waiver of such right or remedy.

(iii) No Assignment: The Lender shall not assign its rights or delegate its duties under this Loan Agreement without the prior written consent of the Borrower.

(iv) No Participation: The Lender shall not participate with any other lender in the financing of the Borrower without the prior written consent of the Borrower.

(v) No Amendment: This Loan Agreement may not be amended or modified except in writing signed by both parties.

(vi) Notices: All notices, requests, and other communications under this Loan Agreement shall be in writing and shall be deemed given upon personal delivery, facsimile transmission, or registered or certified mail, postage prepaid, return receipt requested.

